# .doctrine-forbidden: forbidden identifier patterns
# One ERE regex per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# The doctrine guard (tests/doctrine/doctrine-guard.sh) git-greps each pattern
# against all tracked files and fails if any pattern matches.
#
# Purpose: enforce "nothing here is anonymous / sign the work / stay honest"
# by blocking real infra identifiers, personal hostnames, or IP ranges from
# leaking into tracked files.
#
# Add patterns specific to THIS project. Examples:
#
#   myserver-[0-9]{2}          # internal hostnames
#   10\.255\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+    # LAN IP range
#   mycorp-secret-prefix       # internal project codenames
#
# Leave this file empty (or comments-only) to skip the identifier check.
#
# NOTE: the ai-forge post-generation hook auto-appends workspace
# directory guard patterns below (ERE patterns matching $HOME/<slug>/ and
# ~/<slug>/). Review and remove them if the detected name is generic or shared.
